								<h4>Project Overview</h4>
								<p>Shards of Ylena is a solo action-adventure game prototype in which the player takes on the role of an agile archer. <br>The development has so far focused on building the core player gameplay, including fluid movement mechanics (running, jumping, dodging) and a responsive archery system at the heart of the experience. <br>This project lays the groundwork for a dynamic and strategic gameplay loop within a fantasy world still in early development. It serves as a technical base to experiment with character control, shooting feel, and player responsiveness, ahead of future additions like enemies, special abilities, or an explorable environment.</p>
								
								<h4>Key Features</h4>
								<ul>
									<li>Prototype of a 3D action-adventure game built in Unreal Engine</li>
									<li>Core player movement system: walking, jumping, dodging</li>
									<li>Bow shooting mechanics with basic projectile handling</li>
									<li>Third-person camera system tailored for ranged combat</li>
									<li>Basic environment elements for testing gameplay responsiveness</li>
									<li>Initial groundwork for future abilities (elemental arrows, skills)</li>
									<li>Early-stage animations using AnimBlueprint for movement and aiming</li>
								</ul>
								
